{"id":"mahabharata-1-041","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":41,"title":"एकचत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 41 · Jaratkaru finds his ancestors hanging in a pit","summary":{"en":"Wandering the earth, Jaratkaru sees men hanging head down in a pit by a single tuft of grass that a rat is gnawing. They are the Yayavara sages, his own ancestors, falling because their line is ending, and they beg him to marry and have a son.","kn":"ಭೂಮಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಅಲೆಯುತ್ತಿದ್ದ ಜರತ್ಕಾರು, ಇಲಿ ಕಡಿಯುತ್ತಿರುವ ಒಂದೇ ಹುಲ್ಲಿನ ಕುಚ್ಚನ್ನು ಹಿಡಿದು ಗುಂಡಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ತಲೆಕೆಳಗಾಗಿ ತೂಗುತ್ತಿರುವವರನ್ನು ಕಾಣುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವಂಶ ಕೊನೆಗೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಿರುವುದರಿಂದ ಬೀಳುತ್ತಿರುವ ಯಾಯಾವರ ಋಷಿಗಳಾದ ತನ್ನ ಪಿತೃಗಳು ಅವರು; ಮದುವೆಯಾಗಿ ಮಗನನ್ನು ಪಡೆಯೆಂದು ಬೇಡುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"पृथ्वी पर घूमते हुए जरत्कारु गड्ढे में घास के एक गुच्छे से उलटे लटके लोगों को देखते हैं, जिसे एक चूहा कुतर रहा है। वे यायावर ऋषि, उनके ही पितर हैं, जो वंश समाप्त होने के कारण गिर रहे हैं, और उनसे विवाह कर पुत्र उत्पन्न करने की प्रार्थना करते हैं।","te":"భూమిపై సంచరిస్తున్న జరత్కారుడు, ఎలుక కొరుకుతున్న ఒకే గడ్డిపోచను పట్టుకొని గుంటలో తలక్రిందులుగా వేలాడుతున్నవారిని చూస్తాడు. వంశం అంతరించడం వల్ల పడిపోతున్న యాయావర ఋషులైన తన పితరులే వారు; వివాహం చేసుకొని కుమారుని పొందమని వేడుకుంటారు.","ta":"பூமியில் அலைந்த ஜரத்காரு, எலி கடிக்கும் ஒற்றைப் புல் கொத்தைப் பற்றியபடி குழியில் தலைகீழாகத் தொங்குபவர்களைக் காண்கிறார். வம்சம் முடிவதால் வீழும் யாயாவர முனிவர்களான தம் முன்னோர்களே அவர்கள்; மணம் புரிந்து மகனைப் பெறுமாறு வேண்டுகிறார்கள்.","ml":"ഭൂമിയിൽ അലയുന്ന ജരത്കാരു, ഒരു എലി കടിച്ചുകൊണ്ടിരിക്കുന്ന ഒരു പുല്ലിൻകെട്ടിൽ പിടിച്ച്, കുഴിയിൽ തലകീഴായി തൂങ്ങുന്ന മനുഷ്യരെ കാണുന്നു. സന്താനങ്ങൾ ഇല്ലാതെ വംശം അറ്റുപോകുന്നതിനാൽ വീഴുന്ന തന്റെ പൂർവികരായ യായാവര ഋഷിമാരാണവർ; വിവാഹം കഴിച്ച് പുത്രനെ നൽകണമെന്ന് അവർ അപേക്ഷിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.41; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"आस्तीकपर्व","titleEn":"Astika Parva","verses":[{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta's son said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एतस्मिन्नेव काले तु जरत्कारुर्महातपाः ।\nचचार पृथिवीं कृत्स्नां यत्रसायंगृहो मुनिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At about this time the great ascetic Jaratkaru was wandering the whole earth, a sage who stopped for the night wherever evening found him."}},{"n":2,"text":"चरन्दीक्षां महातेजा दुश्चरामकृतात्मभिः ।\nतीर्थेष्वाप्लवनं कुर्वन्पुण्येषु विचचार ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Observing a vow hard for the unaccomplished to keep, the very brilliant sage bathed at holy tirthas as he roamed."}},{"n":3,"text":"वायुभक्षो निराहारः शुष्यन्नहरहर्मुनिः ।\nस ददर्श पितॄन्गर्ते लम्बमानानधोमुखान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Living on air, without food, drying up day by day, the sage saw his forefathers hanging head down in a pit."}},{"n":4,"text":"एकतन्त्ववशिष्टं वै वीरणस्तम्बमाश्रितान् ।\nतं च तन्तुं शनैराखुमाददानं बिलाश्रयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They hung from a clump of virana grass with only one root-strand left, and a rat that lived in a hole was slowly gnawing that strand."}},{"n":5,"text":"निराहारान्कृशान्दीनान्गर्तेऽऽर्तांस्त्राणमिच्छतः ।\nउपसृत्य स तान्दीनान्दीनरूपोऽभ्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without food, thin, wretched and suffering in the pit, they longed for rescue. Approaching those unfortunate ones, he spoke with a wretched face:"}},{"n":6,"text":"के भवन्तोऽवलम्बन्ते वीरणस्तम्बमाश्रिताः ।\nदुर्बलं खादितैर्मूलैराखुना बिलवासिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who are you hanging here, holding on to a clump of virana grass, whose roots the rat in the hole has eaten, leaving it weak?"}},{"n":7,"text":"वीरणस्तम्बके मूलं यदप्येकमिह स्थितम् ।\nतदप्ययं शनैराखुरादत्ते दशनैः शितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of that clump of grass even the one root still standing here the rat is slowly gnawing away with its sharp teeth."}},{"n":8,"text":"छेत्स्यतेऽल्पावशिष्टत्वादेतदप्यचिरादिव ।\nततः स्थ पतितारोऽत्र गर्ते अस्मिन्नधोमुखाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With so little left it will soon be cut, and then you will fall into this pit head first."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततो मे दुःखमुत्पन्नं दृष्ट्वा युष्मानधोमुखान् ।\nकृच्छ्रामापदमापन्नान्प्रियं किं करवाणि वः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing you in this extreme peril, head down, sorrow has come to me. What can I do to please you?"}},{"n":10,"text":"तपसोऽस्य चतुर्थेन तृतीयेनापि वा पुनः ।\nअर्धेन वापि निस्तर्तुमापदं ब्रूत माचिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me quickly whether you can be rescued from this danger with a quarter of my austerity, a third, or even half."}},{"n":11,"text":"अथ वापि समग्रेण तरन्तु तपसा मम ।\nभवन्तः सर्व एवास्मात्काममेवं विधीयताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or let all of you cross over with all of my austerity. Do whatever is fitting in this way.\""}},{"text":"पितर ऊचुः","meaning":{"en":"The forefathers said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"ऋद्धो भवान्ब्रह्मचारी यो नस्त्रातुमिहेच्छति ।\nन तु विप्राग्र्य तपसा शक्यमेतद्व्यपोहितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You are a wealthy celibate, who wish to rescue us here, but this cannot be undone with austerity, best of brahmins."}},{"n":13,"text":"अस्ति नस्तात तपसः फलं प्रवदतां वर ।\nसंतानप्रक्षयाद्ब्रह्मन्पतामो निरयेऽशुचौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"We have the fruit of austerity, dear one, best of speakers, but with our line cut off, brahmin, we fall into a foul hell."}},{"n":14,"text":"लम्बतामिह नस्तात न ज्ञानं प्रतिभाति वै ।\nयेन त्वां नाभिजानीमो लोके विख्यातपौरुषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As we hang here, dear one, our understanding does not shine, so that we do not recognize you, though your manliness is famed in the world."}},{"n":15,"text":"ऋद्धो भवान्महाभागो यो नः शोच्यान्सुदुःखितान् ।\nशोचस्युपेत्य कारुण्याच्छृणु ये वै वयं द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are fortunate and great, to feel compassion and grieve for us, who are pitiable and in great misery. Hear who we are, brahmin."}},{"n":16,"text":"यायावरा नाम वयमृषयः संशितव्रताः ।\nलोकात्पुण्यादिह भ्रष्टाः संतानप्रक्षयाद्विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"We are sages named Yayavara, strict in our vows. By the end of our line we have fallen from the world of merit, lord."}},{"n":17,"text":"प्रनष्टं नस्तपः पुण्यं न हि नस्तन्तुरस्ति वै ।\nअस्ति त्वेकोऽद्य नस्तन्तुः सोऽपि नास्ति यथा तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Our merit from austerity is lost, for we have no thread left. One thread remains to us, yet he is as good as not there."}},{"n":18,"text":"मन्दभाग्योऽल्पभाग्यानां बन्धुः स किल नः कुले ।\nजरत्कारुरिति ख्यातो वेदवेदाङ्गपारगः ।\nनियतात्मा महात्मा च सुव्रतः सुमहातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In our family there is one unlucky man, kin to us unlucky ones, named Jaratkaru, who has mastered the Vedas and Vedangas, self-controlled, great-souled, of good vows and great austerity."}},{"n":19,"text":"तेन स्म तपसो लोभात्कृच्छ्रमापादिता वयम् ।\nन तस्य भार्या पुत्रो वा बान्धवो वास्ति कश्चन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Out of greed for austerity he has brought us to this misery. He has no wife, no son, no relatives at all."}},{"n":20,"text":"तस्माल्लम्बामहे गर्ते नष्टसंज्ञा ह्यनाथवत् ।\nस वक्तव्यस्त्वया दृष्ट्वा अस्माकं नाथवत्तया ॥","meaning":{"en":"So we hang in this pit, senseless, as though without a protector. If you see him, tell him on our behalf, as if you were our protector:"}},{"n":21,"text":"पितरस्तेऽवलम्बन्ते गर्ते दीना अधोमुखाः ।\nसाधु दारान्कुरुष्वेति प्रजायस्वेति चाभिभो ।\nकुलतन्तुर्हि नः शिष्टस्त्वमेवैकस्तपोधन ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Your forefathers are hanging in a pit, wretched and head down. Be good, take a wife and beget children, mighty one. You alone, ascetic, are the thread left to our line.'"}},{"n":22,"text":"यं तु पश्यसि नो ब्रह्मन्वीरणस्तम्बमाश्रितान् ।\nएषोऽस्माकं कुलस्तम्ब आसीत्स्वकुलवर्धनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The clump of virana you see us holding, brahmin, was our family's stock, which made our line grow."}},{"n":23,"text":"यानि पश्यसि वै ब्रह्मन्मूलानीहास्य वीरुधः ।\nएते नस्तन्तवस्तात कालेन परिभक्षिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The roots of this plant that you see, brahmin, are our threads, eaten away in time."}},{"n":24,"text":"यत्त्वेतत्पश्यसि ब्रह्मन्मूलमस्यार्धभक्षितम् ।\nतत्र लम्बामहे सर्वे सोऽप्येकस्तप आस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The half-eaten root you see, brahmin, is where we all hang, and that is the one man left, devoted to austerity."}},{"n":25,"text":"यमाखुं पश्यसि ब्रह्मन्काल एष महाबलः ।\nस तं तपोरतं मन्दं शनैः क्षपयते तुदन् ।\nजरत्कारुं तपोलुब्धं मन्दात्मानमचेतसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The rat you see, brahmin, is mighty Time. He is slowly grinding that dull ascetic down, Jaratkaru, greedy for austerity, slow of mind and heedless."}},{"n":26,"text":"न हि नस्तत्तपस्तस्य तारयिष्यति सत्तम ।\nछिन्नमूलान्परिभ्रष्टान्कालोपहतचेतसः ।\nनरकप्रतिष्ठान्पश्यास्मान्यथा दुष्कृतिनस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"His austerity will not save us, good sir. See us with roots cut, fallen, our minds struck by Time, standing in hell like sinners."}},{"n":27,"text":"अस्मासु पतितेष्वत्र सह पूर्वैः पितामहैः ।\nछिन्नः कालेन सोऽप्यत्र गन्ता वै नरकं ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When we have fallen here with the ancestors before us, he will also be cut off by Time and go to hell."}},{"n":28,"text":"तपो वाप्यथ वा यज्ञो यच्चान्यत्पावनं महत् ।\nतत्सर्वं न समं तात संतत्येति सतां मतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Austerity, sacrifice, or whatever else great and purifying: none of it equals offspring, as the good hold."}},{"n":29,"text":"स तात दृष्ट्वा ब्रूयास्त्वं जरत्कारुं तपस्विनम् ।\nयथादृष्टमिदं चास्मै त्वयाख्येयमशेषतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear one, if you see the ascetic Jaratkaru, tell him all that you have seen here without omission."}},{"n":30,"text":"यथा दारान्प्रकुर्यात्स पुत्रांश्चोत्पादयेद्यथा ।\nतथा ब्रह्मंस्त्वया वाच्यः सोऽस्माकं नाथवत्तया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell him as our protector, brahmin, so that he takes a wife and begets sons.\""}}]}]}